{"study_accession":"PRJNA1366709","secondary_study_accession":"SRP647670","title":"FluPRINT Study: Characterisation of the Immune and Transcriptional Response to LAIV","description":"The development of universal influenza vaccines requires eliciting durable T stem cell-like memory (TSCM) responses, yet the baseline determinants governing TSCM expansion remain undefined. Here, using multi-omic systems immunology in a pediatric cohort immunized with live attenuated influenza vaccine (LAIV), we identify a pre-existing state of innate antiviral readiness as the master determinant of vaccine-mediated TSCM induction. This submission contains the baseline (Visit 1) whole-blood transcriptional profiles of 19 healthy children (ages 4-6) prior to vaccination. Overall design: Whole blood samples were collected from healthy children (4-6 years old) at baseline (Visit 1) prior to administration of the live attenuated influenza vaccine (LAIV). Total RNA was extracted and sequenced to identify pre-existing transcriptional signatures associated with subsequent vaccine responses.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":19,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN53319894","study_accession":"PRJNA1366709","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"Whole Blood Transcriptome Baseline D33V1","description":"Whole Blood Transcriptome Baseline D33V1","sex":"female","geo_sample":"GSM9304963","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-11-23","attributes":[["source_name","whole blood"],["tissue","whole blood"],["age","5"],["sex","female"],["group","2"],["treatment","Baseline (Pre-vaccination)"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR36135335","experiment_accession":"SRX31176593","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":19676068,"base_count":5942172536,"first_public":"2025-11-23","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 4000 sequencing: GSM9304963: Whole Blood